# Only web/ is deployed, plus the one file the Dockerfile reaches outside it.
#
# `runs/` with a trailing slash excludes the directory itself, and a negation
# cannot re-include a file inside a directory that is never walked into — so
# `!runs/archive.json` under `runs/` silently did nothing, the COPY found no
# file, and the deploy failed while the previous one kept serving. The glob form
# excludes the contents rather than the directory, which is what makes the
# negation reachable.
runs/*
!runs/archive.json
benchmarks/
.cache/
tests/
docs/
scripts/
rsi_arena/
harnesses/
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
